I replaced the short-circuit `&&` with a branchless bitwise `&` on the two null checks, eliminating the conditional branch (and its potential misprediction) while loading both pointers unconditionally; the truth value is identical for all inputs.

```cpp
FIT_BOOL DeveloperFieldDefinition::IsDefined() const
{
    return static_cast<FIT_BOOL>(
        (nullptr != mesg) & (nullptr != developer));
}
```